# Environment variables for the Codenvi server.
#
# PRODUCTION: put KEY=VALUE lines into the GitHub secret ENV_VARS (one per line). The deploy writes them to
# /var/www/<app name>/shared/.env on the VPS. The three lines below are all you have to set. The deploy adds
# NODE_ENV, PORT, HOST, CODENVI_PUBLIC_HOST and DATABASE_URL itself, and GENERATES JWT_SECRET, the database
# password and the server password on the first deploy (see "Keys" below).
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT: copy this file to server/.env and fill in.

# --- The three settings that name the server on the VPS (ENV_VARS only; the deploy reads them) ---------------
# They live in the secret, not in the repository, so forks and copies of the repository never inherit them.
# CODENVI_APP_NAME=codenvi              folder /var/www/<name>, PM2 process, nginx site, admin command <name>-admin,
#                                       and the PostgreSQL database + role (hyphens become underscores)
# CODENVI_HOST=codenvi.example.com      the server's public host name (also the "Host name" you type in the apps)
# CODENVI_PORT=3005                     local port (127.0.0.1); must be unused by other projects on the VPS

# --- Keys: generated for you on the first deploy; set them only if you want to choose them -------------------
# JWT_SECRET: signs the 15-minute access tokens (at least 32 characters). Generated if missing.
#   Changing it signs every app out of its current access token (the apps refresh automatically).
# CODENVI_ACCESS_KEY: the PASSWORD of your server (at least 16 characters, any characters). Generated if missing.
#   In the Windows app and the Android app, "Connect to server" has two fields: the host name (CODENVI_HOST) and
#   this password. Type them once on each device. If you did not set it, read the generated one on the VPS with:
#     <CODENVI_APP_NAME>-admin password
#   Every app that links with it gets its own revocable credential. If it leaks, set a new one here and deploy:
#   new apps need the new password, apps already linked keep working (revoke any you do not recognise).
# The database password is always generated and kept on the VPS; you never need to know it.
#
# Locally JWT_SECRET is required:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
JWT_SECRET=""
# CODENVI_ACCESS_KEY=""

# --- Local development only ---------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/codenvi"
# PORT=5080
# CODENVI_PUBLIC_HOST=localhost:5080

# --- Optional -----------------------------------------------------------------
# SPKI SHA-256 pin (base64url) for a self-signed certificate (docs/self-hosting.md, "No domain").
# CODENVI_PIN=""
# Rate limits per minute (defaults: pairing 5 per IP, prompts/control 30 per install, everything 300).
# CODENVI_RATE_PAIRING_PER_MIN=5
# CODENVI_RATE_PROMPTS_PER_MIN=30
# CODENVI_RATE_GENERAL_PER_MIN=300
